     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\": 3, \"rationale\": \"Blocking 3 steps is enough: mailArchive:collection, codeRepo:collection and vpnSession:authenticate. Blocking vpnSession:authenticate cuts off hypervisor:privilegeEscalation, so vaultRead:collection is unreachable. It also cuts off serviceAccount:privilegeEscalation, so dbReplica:collection is unreachable. With mailArchive:collection and codeRepo:collection also blocked, all four parents of the target are gone. Fewer than 3 cannot work because there are three attack routes that share no blockable step. Route 1: exposedApi -> tokenCache -> monitoringHost -> mailArchive. Route 2: internet -> sshKey -> printServer -> codeRepo. Route 3: browserStore and mailClient -> vpnSession, plus browserStore and ciRunner -> rdpLogin, both feeding hypervisor -> vaultRead. Each route reaches the target on its own, so each needs at least one separate block.\"}"
    }
   ],
